# Android String Resources

- Declare every new user-facing string, including button labels, titles, messages, and descriptions, in `res/values/strings.xml`.
- In Jetpack Compose, reference these resources with `stringResource(R.string.<name>)` instead of hardcoding the text in Kotlin.
- Use descriptive `snake_case` resource names and add format placeholders to the resource when a string contains dynamic values.
- Do not extract non-user-facing technical values or genuinely dynamic content into string resources.
